   Make sure to name the class after the browser you're testing (`FirefoxTester` in this example).

   Also, note that we're setting the binary for Firefox to use Safari Technology Preview, which is the only way to use Dusk for testing Safari. 3. Use the new test case: To run your tests with Firefox, simply change the command in the terminal to use the new test case:

   ```bash
   vendor/bin/dusk browser:firefox test App\Testing\Browser\FirefoxTester
   ```

   Similarly, for Safari:

   ```bash
   vendor/bin/dusk browser:headless_safari test App\Testing\Browser\FirefoxTester
   ```

   Here, `headless_safari` is just another_browser:identifier which you can use in place of `chrome` or `firefox`. To use `headless_safari` you need to also configure your `.env` file with the `HEADLESS_SAFARI=true` option.

